```java
public static String reverse(String input) {
    if (input == null) return null;
    char[] chars = input.toCharArray();
    int left = 0, right = chars.length - 1;
    while (left < right) {
        char temp = chars[left];
        chars[left] = chars[right];
        chars[right] = temp;
        left++;
        right--;
    }
    return new String(chars);
}
```

This method handles `null` inputs gracefully and uses a two-pointer approach to reverse the character array in place, then returns a new string. It is efficient with O(n) time and space complexity.

